Theorem TF-N-A: RcInc + RcDec side-effect-only confirmation (no dst, no demand)

  Preconditions:
    - Instructions are `RcInc { var }` and `RcDec { var }` per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A + Appendix A rows 16 + 17
    - Per Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A: "Side-effect-only: `RcInc`/`RcDec`
      (no `dst`)."
    - Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 backward-demand table row for
      `RcInc`/`RcDec`: "none (RC operation, not a use)"
    - Appendix A rows 16 + 17 carry "—" across every per-dimension column
    - The side-effect-only ArcInstr set is RcInc + RcDec EXCLUSIVELY per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A. Burden-tracking-plan instructions
      (BurdenInc / BurdenDec) are Phase-5/Phase-6 architecture under the
      separate burden-tracking plan; their TF-shape soundness ties to
      §11 coexistence handshake CH theorems (CH-2 + CH-3), NOT §04
      TF-N/A.

  Soundness property:
    Forall arc_instr in {RcInc { var }, RcDec { var }}.
      transfer_tf_n_a(arc_instr) = NoDst (no AimsState emitted)
      AND backward_demand_tf_n_a(arc_instr) = empty (no TF-11 demand)
    AND L-6 layer (b) monotonicity holds vacuously — no output state to
    monotone over, no demand to accumulate via TF-11 seq_add.

  Proof obligation:
    Four-part discharge:
      (a) RcInc no-dst confirmation — verify TF-N/A for RcInc emits
          NoDst per Appendix A row 16. The state map MUST NOT acquire
          a new entry.
      (b) RcDec no-dst confirmation — verify TF-N/A for RcDec emits
          NoDst per Appendix A row 17.
      (c) No backward TF-11 demand confirmation — per Annex E §AIMS
          TF-11 table: "RcInc/RcDec { var }: none (RC operation, not a
          use)." Verified: backward_demand_tf_n_a() returns empty for
          both variants.
      (d) Burden-op exclusion confirmation — verify the side-effect-
          only set is RcInc + RcDec exclusively; BurdenInc and BurdenDec
          are out-of-scope per Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A + the burden-
          tracking plan §06 mechanical-lowering contract (proven at
          §11 CH theorems).

    Part (a) — RcInc no-dst confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A + Appendix A row 16:
        RcInc | TF-N/A | — | — | — | — | — | — | —
      Verified: transfer_tf_n_a("RcInc") returns NoDst marker.
      Semantics: RcInc { var } physically increments `var`'s reference
      count by 1 (writes to the RC header memory cell). The AIMS-level
      transfer is empty because (i) no new SSA value is defined, and
      (ii) the operation reads `var` for its address but does NOT
      consume `var`'s value as a TF-11-style "use" — `var` retains its
      AimsState unchanged.

    Part (b) — RcDec no-dst confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A + Appendix A row 17:
        RcDec | TF-N/A | — | — | — | — | — | — | —
      Verified: transfer_tf_n_a("RcDec") returns NoDst marker.
      Semantics: RcDec { var } physically decrements `var`'s reference
      count by 1 (potentially triggers deallocation if count hits 0).
      Same forward-transfer rationale as RcInc: no new SSA value;
      `var`'s AimsState unchanged at AIMS layer.

    Part (c) — no backward TF-11 demand:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11 table:
        RcInc/RcDec { var } | none (RC operation, not a use)
      Verified: backward_demand_tf_n_a("RcInc") = empty list;
      backward_demand_tf_n_a("RcDec") = empty list.
      Rationale: TF-11 emits backward demand on operands that REPRESENT
      A USE of a runtime value. RC operations manipulate the RC header
      directly (a memory-management side-effect, not a value-consuming
      use); demand-tracking does NOT see them as uses. Note this is
      consistent with RL-22 (RC-motion safety) — RcInc/RcDec are NOT
      RC-observable barriers FOR `v` themselves in the demand sense;
      the barrier semantics live at RL-22 + RL-26, separate from TF-11
      demand emission.

    Part (d) — Burden-op exclusion:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-N/A: "Side-effect-only: `RcInc`/`RcDec`
      (no `dst`)." The side-effect-only ArcInstr SET (the cardinality
      of the TF-N/A row in Appendix A) is exactly 2: RcInc + RcDec.
      Verified: TF-N/A enumeration produces a 2-element set.
      Burden-tracking-plan instructions (BurdenInc / BurdenDec at
      docs/ori_lang/proposals/approved/aims-burden-tracking-proposal.md)
      are NOT members of the §04 TF-N/A set; their TF-shape soundness
      lives at §11 coexistence handshake (CH-2 + CH-3 theorems
      composed with predicate-stack-derived burden-ops). §04 proves
      the canonical AIMS calculus only.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — vacuous L-6 layer (b) discharge for
        side-effect-only instructions per
        section_04::verify_tf_n_a_side_effect_only)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A rows 16 + 17 "—" enumeration
        + RcInc/RcDec 2-element set verification per
        section_04::verify_tf_n_a_side_effect_only)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no codomain element)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no dst, no refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-N/A via RcInc + RcDec no-dst confirmation + no-TF-11-demand confirmation + Appendix A "—" enumeration + Burden-op exclusion confirmation
